  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#scriptTag\r\n\r\n> A start tag whose tag name is \"template\"\r\n> Insert an HTML element for the token\\.\r\n> \r\n> Insert a marker at the end of the list of active formatting elements\\.\r\n> \r\n> Set the frameset\\-ok flag to \"not ok\"\\.\r\n\r\nSee http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/5470\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<head><template></template></head><p><frameset>\r\n```\r\n\r\nAFAICT from the spec, the `<template>` start tag in \"in head\" sets frameset-ok to \"not ok\", then `<p>` in \"after head\" will insert a `body` element and switch to \"in body\" and reprocess the `<p>`, then the `<frameset>` in \"in body\" should be ignored because frameset-ok is \"not ok\".\r\n\r\nRight?\r\n\r\nGecko/Chromium/WebKit/Edge end up with a `frameset` element in the DOM for the above, so maybe template-in-head shouldn't flip the flag.\r\n\r\ncc @whatwg/html-parser ",
